sn11.20:8.1 starts: Matali: “‘Those whom you worship,
mn108:4.1 starts: So the venerable Ānanda went to the brahmin Gopaka Moggallāna
mn108:5.2 starts: “There is no single bhikkhu, brahmin, who possesses in each and every way
mn108:11.2 starts: “There is a single bhikkhu, brahmin, whom we now honour, respect
mn108:12.6 starts: When you were asked: ‘Is there, Master Ānanda, any single bhikkhu whom you honour
mn108:25.5 starts: “Indeed, brahmin, that the Bamboo Grove is pleasant…
mn108:25.7 starts: The worthy ones are meditators and cultivate meditation.
mn108:27.3 starts: With the stilling of applied and sustained thought,
# superseded: mn108:27.4 starts: he enters upon and abides in the second jhāna…With the fading
# superseded: mn108:27.5 starts: With the abandoning of pleasure and pain…
mn108:27.6 starts: The Blessed One praised that kind of meditation.”
sn16.9:1.3 starts: Kassapa too, to whatever extent he wishes, secluded from sensual pleasures
sn16.9:2.1 starts: “Bhikkhus, to whatever extent I wish, with the subsiding of thought
sn16.9:2.2 starts: Kassapa too, to whatever extent he wishes, with the subsiding
sn16.9:3.1 starts: “Bhikkhus, to whatever extent I wish, with the fading away
sn16.9:3.2 starts: Kassapa too, to whatever extent he wishes, enters and dwells in the third
sn16.9:4.1 starts: “Bhikkhus, to whatever extent I wish, with the abandoning of pleasure
sn16.9:4.2 starts: Kassapa too, to whatever extent he wishes, enters and dwells in the fourth
sn16.9:5.1 starts: “Bhikkhus, to whatever extent I wish, with the complete transcendence
sn16.9:9.2 starts: Kassapa too, to whatever extent he wishes, enters and dwells in the cessation
sn16.9:10.1 starts: “Bhikkhus, to whatever extent I wish, I wield the various
sn16.9:10.2 starts: Kassapa too, to whatever extent he wishes, wields the various
sn16.9:11.1 starts: “Bhikkhus, to whatever extent I wish, with the divine ear
sn16.9:11.2 starts: Kassapa too, to whatever extent he wishes, with the divine ear
sn16.9:13.2 starts: Kassapa too, to whatever extent he wishes, recollects his manifold
sn16.9:14.1 starts: “Bhikkhus, to whatever extent I wish, with the divine eye
sn16.9:14.2 starts: Kassapa too, to whatever extent he wishes, with the divine eye
sn16.9:15.1 starts: “Bhikkhus, by the destruction of the taints, in this very life
sn16.9:15.2 starts: Kassapa too, by the destruction of the taints
